666	 * Compared by serialization rather than by reference or by `updatedAt`.
667	 *
668	 * The rows come from IndexedDB and are rebuilt the same way every time, so
669	 * key order is stable and this is reliable in the direction that matters: two
670	 * different values never compare equal. The worst a false difference can do is
671	 * send a row that did not need sending, which is what the old code did to
672	 * every row on every push.
